    "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes #40393.\n\nOn v0.5.20, serving a DeepSeek-family / GLM MLA checkpoint with `--quantization humming` crashes on every TP rank at the end of weight loading:\n\n```\nAttributeError: 'BlockQuantScaleParameter' object has no attribute 'format_ue8m0'\n```\n\n#38446 hoisted the `format_ue8m0` attribute read out of a short-circuit expression in `DeepseekV2WeightLoaderMixin.post_load_weights`, so it is now evaluated unconditionally. The attribute is only stamped by quant methods that requant scales to UE8M0 (fp8/DeepGEMM, flashinfer_trtllm, mega_moe, NPU methods); quant methods like `humming` never stamp it, so the read genuinely fails there.\n\n## Modifications\n\n`python/sglang/srt/models/deepseek_common/deepseek_weight_loader.py` — guard **both** unguarded reads with `getattr(..., False)`:\n\n1. `is_ue8m0_uint8 = weight_scale.format_ue8m0 and ...` (line 632)\n2. the `should_deepgemm_weight_requant_ue8m0(...)` branch (line 656), which is still reachable after (1) is fixed: when DeepGEMM UE8M0 requant is enabled (H100/H20, 128×128 block size) the condition evaluates `weight_scale.format_ue8m0` and raises the same `AttributeError` — fixing site (1) alone only relocates the crash 24 lines down.\n\nThe `getattr(..., False)` pattern matches existing defensive usage in `layers/linear.py` and `models/qwen3_5.py`. Behavior for quant methods that DO stamp the attribute is unchanged — the default `False` only applies where the attribute never existed.\n\n### Relation to #40397\n\nPR #40397 fixes the first read (site 1). As described above, the second read (site 2) is evaluated when the `elif should_deepgemm_weight_requant_ue8m0(...)` branch is taken, which is the common case on H100/H20 — so that PR alone still crashes for `--quantization humming`. This PR covers both sites; the audit is straightforward to re-verify: these are the only two non-defensive `format_ue8m0` reads in the repo (all other sites are writes/`getattr`).\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nN/A — the change only affects quant methods that never had the attribute (where loading previously crashed); methods that stamp `format_ue8m0` take the same code path as before.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A — weight-loading-time code only, no runtime path touched.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40351378538](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40351378538)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40351378452](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40351378452)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40351380275](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40351380275)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
